{
  "id": "sliding-window-maximum",
  "questionId": "sliding-window-maximum",
  "slug": "sliding-window-maximum",
  "title": "Sliding Window Maximum",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "category": "Sliding window",
  "patterns": [
    "sliding window",
    "monotonic deque",
    "fixed-size window"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "rescanning all k elements for every window wastes work - if you already knew the max of the previous window, could you avoid recomputing it from scratch?",
    "what if you kept a running list of 'still possibly the max' candidates, and threw away any candidate that could never win again? if a number is smaller than a number to its right, can it ever be the max of a window that contains both?",
    "keep a deque of indices with decreasing values: before adding a new index, pop from the back any indices whose values are smaller than the new one (they can never be the max again)",
    "the front of the deque is always the current window's max - just also remember to pop it from the front once it slides outside the window's left edge"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "storing values in the deque instead of indices, making it impossible to tell when the max has slid out of the window",
    "forgetting to remove the front of the deque when its index falls outside the current window",
    "popping in the wrong direction, or not maintaining the decreasing order invariant when inserting a new index"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of integers and a window size `k`.\n\n**As the window of size k slides from the start of the array to the end, one step at a time, return the maximum value inside the window at each position.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums.length <= 10^5",
      "-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4",
      "1 <= k <= nums.length"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "k equals the array length (only one window, its own max)",
      "k = 1 (the answer is just the array itself)",
      "strictly increasing or strictly decreasing values"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
